extends /views/templates/layouts/_base

append variables
	- pagetitle = "Chart types | Additional types"
	- pagedescription = "The additional chart types of Tablechart, such as the scatter chart, and how to load them."

block content
	.lane
		.container
			.page-header
				h1 Additional types

	+section("The additional types")
		p The main script has the column, bar, line, area, waterfall and donut charts. The additional types are in a separate script. Maybe you do not need it, then you do not need to load it. The stylesheet is the same for all.

		p Right now, only the 'Scatter' chart is in the additional chart types. More types may be added in the future.

		table
			thead
				tr
					th Type
					th Name
			tbody
				tr
					td: a(href=url('/types/scatter.html')) Scatter
					td: code scatter

	+section("With a build tool")
		p If you use a build tool, import the type from #[code @martinomagnifico/tablechart/additional-types], and add it with #[code addType()] before #[code init()] or #[code create()]. The first argument is the value of #[code data-chart].

		+codeblock('JS').
			import { addType, init } from "@martinomagnifico/tablechart";
			import { scatter } from "@martinomagnifico/tablechart/additional-types";

			addType("scatter", scatter);
			init();

		p Only the types you import are in your bundle.

	+section("With a script tag")
		p If you use a script tag, load #[code tablechart-additional-types.js] after #[code tablechart.js]. It adds all the additional types. It uses the code in #[code tablechart.js], so that code is not loaded twice.

		+codeblock('HTML').
			<link rel="stylesheet" href="tablechart.css">
			<script src="tablechart.js"></script>
			<script src="tablechart-additional-types.js"></script>
			<script>
				Tablechart.init();
			</script>

	+section("If a type is not added")
		p If a chart has a type that is not added, the chart is not made. The console then lists the types that are there.

	+section("Next")
		p See #[a(href=url('/reference/api.html#addtype')) addType()] in the API.
